// Model-output: Claude Fable 5

Build tig from https://github.com/ludios/tig (the syntax-highlighting fork)
with the tig-syntax-filter daemon and client included.

Apply from the nixpkgs root (the patch lives in the tig repository):

  git apply /path/to/tig/doc/slop/nixpkgs.patch
  # or: patch -p1 < /path/to/tig/doc/slop/nixpkgs.patch

Two hashes are lib.fakeHash placeholders (src and pnpmDeps): run a build,
copy the real hash from each mismatch error, repeat once.  Also consider
pinning `rev` to a commit of the `prime` branch instead of the branch name
so later pushes don't invalidate the src hash.

The result installs `tig` (wrapped so a bare `tig-syntax-filter` in tigrc
resolves), the C client, a `tig-syntax-daemon` launcher pinned to
nodejs_24, the daemon sources + production node_modules under
lib/tig-syntax-filter/, and contrib/tig-syntax.tigrc under etc/.

--- a/pkgs/by-name/ti/tig/package.nix	2026-08-08 00:48:57.701081449 +0000
+++ b/pkgs/by-name/ti/tig/package.nix	2026-08-08 01:01:37.066117864 +0000
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
